{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit maximum and annual increase cap","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit of more than one and one-half times one month's rent, and any yearly increase of an existing deposit may not exceed 10% of the current deposit. Collecting a deposit is optional.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; yearly increase max 10% of current deposit","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey where the landlord collects a security deposit; a landlord is not required to collect one.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month's rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit held in trust in an insured New Jersey account","requirement":"Security deposit money remains the tenant's property and must be held in trust, not commingled with the landlord's assets; it must be deposited in an insured New Jersey bank in an interest-bearing account, with a money market option for landlords of 10 or more units.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Security deposit money received for residential units; landlords or designees receiving deposits for ten or less units must use an insured New Jersey interest-bearing account.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days for residential purposes by a person having a permanent residence elsewhere; not seasonal, temporary or migrant farm worker housing.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"A landlord or designee who receives security deposit money for ten or less units must deposit that money in an insured bank or savings and loan association located in New Jersey in an interest-bearing account at the current interest rate at the time of deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit interest belongs to the tenant","requirement":"Interest or earnings on a security deposit belong to the tenant and must be paid in cash or credited toward rent on the renewal or anniversary of the lease, or on January 31 if the landlord has given written notice of that payment date.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Security deposits held under the New Jersey Security Deposit Law.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"The interest or earnings paid on the security deposit belongs to the tenant and shall be paid to the tenant in cash or credited toward rent due and owing on the renewal or anniversary of the tenant's lease or on January 31, if the tenant has been given written notice, that the interest payments will be paid on January 31 of each year (N.J.S.A. 46:8-19 (c)).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Deposit account notice and tenant remedy of applying deposit plus 7% to rent","requirement":"The landlord must tell the tenant in writing where the deposit is held, the amount, account type and interest rate within 30 days of receipt and at each annual interest payment; if proper notice is not given or interest is unpaid, the tenant may apply the deposit plus 7% interest to rent.","key_value":"7% per annum","coverage_conditions":"Security deposits subject to the Security Deposit Law, including money transferred to a new landlord or moved to another account or bank.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19.1","quoted_span":"If a tenant does not receive proper notice or is not paid interest as required, the tenant may use the security deposit for payment of rent by giving the landlord written notice that the security money plus interest at the rate of 7% per annum be applied to rent payments or payments due or to become due from the tenant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return within 30 days of tenancy end","requirement":"Within 30 days after a tenancy ends, the landlord must return the deposit plus interest less lawful deductions and send an itemized list of deductions by registered or certified mail; a tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld.","key_value":"30 days; double damages","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies where a security deposit was collected; deductions may cover damages beyond normal wear and tear and other money due under the lease.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after displacement by fire, flood or condemnation","requirement":"When a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation, the landlord must return the security deposit within five business days and let the tenant know within three business days where the deposit can be collected.","key_value":"5 business days","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies where the tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation, once an official posts a no-occupancy notice or certifies displacement beyond seven days.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within five (5) business days after a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation, or evacuation, the landlord must return the security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after domestic-violence lease termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence, the landlord must make the deposit, plus interest, available within 15 business days and notify the tenant in writing within three business days where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence; transient or seasonal rentals are excluded.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant's security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant's agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Cap on upfront charges at the inception of a lease","requirement":"At the inception of a lease a landlord may require no more than one and one-half times the monthly rent as security plus the first month's rent, no more than two and one-half times the monthly rent in total; prepaid funds securing future rent count as deposit.","key_value":"2.5 months' rent total upfront","coverage_conditions":"All New Jersey residential leases at inception; courts treat advanced rent above one and one-half times the monthly rent as part of the security deposit.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"That means the landlord may not require more than two and one-half times the monthly rent at the inception of the lease, this includes the security deposit and the first month's rent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
